(7b) Sec 5.2's stated Stirling mechanism: 'the factor 2^{b+1} in 2^N exactly
     cancels the 2^{-(b+1)} in the prefactor r!(r+b)!/(2r+b+1)!'.
     The prefactor contains NO power of 2.  The real cancellation is
       rho_b(r) := 2^b [(r+b)!/r!] [(2r+1)!/(2r+b+1)!] = prod_j (2r+2j)/(2r+j+1) -> 1
        b=1 r=10      rho_b(r)=1.0000000000   1+b(b-1)/(4r)=1.0000000000
        b=1 r=1000    rho_b(r)=1.0000000000   1+b(b-1)/(4r)=1.0000000000
        b=1 r=100000  rho_b(r)=1.0000000000   1+b(b-1)/(4r)=1.0000000000
        b=2 r=10      rho_b(r)=1.0434782609   1+b(b-1)/(4r)=1.0500000000
        b=2 r=1000    rho_b(r)=1.0004992511   1+b(b-1)/(4r)=1.0005000000
        b=2 r=100000  rho_b(r)=1.0000049999   1+b(b-1)/(4r)=1.0000050000
        b=3 r=10      rho_b(r)=1.1304347826   1+b(b-1)/(4r)=1.1500000000
        b=3 r=1000    rho_b(r)=1.0014977534   1+b(b-1)/(4r)=1.0015000000
        b=3 r=100000  rho_b(r)=1.0000149998   1+b(b-1)/(4r)=1.0000150000
        b=5 r=10      rho_b(r)=1.4608695652   1+b(b-1)/(4r)=1.5000000000
        b=5 r=1000    rho_b(r)=1.0049962463   1+b(b-1)/(4r)=1.0050000000
        b=5 r=100000  rho_b(r)=1.0000499996   1+b(b-1)/(4r)=1.0000500000

